# Frontend Conventions

## Components

- **Only** import UI primitives from `@/components/ui/` — never from `reka-ui` directly in pages
- Use `<Button>`, `<Input>`, `<Card>`, `<Separator>`, `<Badge>` etc. from shadcn-vue
- Layout components: `AppLayout`, `AuthLayout`, `AdminLayout`, `SettingsLayout`
- Wrap every layout root with `<BrandProvider>` so DB brand colors apply

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input';
</script>

<!-- ❌ BAD — importing Reka directly in a page -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { Button } from 'reka-ui';
</script>
```

## Composables for settings

Always use composables — never read `usePage().props` directly for app settings:

```ts
// ✅
const { appName, logoUrl, primaryColor } = useBranding();
const { currentLocale, supportedLocales } = useLocalization();
const { zohoEnabled, passwordLoginEnabled } = useAuthSettings();
const { defaultAppearance, forceAppearance } = useThemeSettings();

// ❌
const appName = usePage().props.appSettings.branding.appName;
```

## i18n

- Use `useI18n()` from `vue-i18n` for all user-facing strings
- Add new strings to ALL locale files (`lang/en.json`, `fr.json`, `es.json`, `ar.json`)

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n';
const { t } = useI18n();
</script>

<template>
  <Button>{{ t('auth.login') }}</Button>
</template>
```

## Appearance

- Dark mode is toggled by `.dark` class on `<html>` — never manually add/remove
- Use `useAppearance()` composable to read/set theme
- Pass `{ defaultAppearance, forceAppearance }` options from `useThemeSettings()`

## Navigation

- Internal links → `<Link href="...">` from `@inertiajs/vue3`
- Named routes → Wayfinder helpers: `import { dashboard } from '@/routes'`
- External links → regular `<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">`

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` is enforced — no `any`, no `// @ts-ignore`
- Shared Inertia page props are typed via `declare module '@inertiajs/core'` in `global.d.ts`
- New shared props require a matching type in `resources/js/types/`

## Icons

- **Only `lucide-vue-next`** — never use heroicons, fontawesome, or any other icon library
- Import icons by name: `import { Languages, Settings2, LayoutGrid } from 'lucide-vue-next'`
- Use semantic icon names that match intent (e.g. `<Languages />` for locale, `<Moon />` for dark mode)
- Size via Tailwind: `class="size-4"` (not `width`/`height` props)

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<Languages class="size-4 text-muted-foreground" />

<!-- ❌ BAD — wrong library -->
<HeroIcon name="globe" />
```

## Styling

- All colors via Tailwind semantic utilities (`text-primary`, `bg-background`, `border-border`)
- Avoid hardcoded hex values — use CSS custom properties: `var(--primary)`
- `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging
